walkthrough "linux-zorin - sshd"
resolution 1920x1080
recording_resolution 1920x1080
# THE ACCOUNT THIS DISK HAS IS `vmuser` - see the manjaro header for the measurement.
#
# ubiquity fills the username from the full name as it is typed, so its two `type:` steps
# APPEND and the account is created with the value twice.
# `ssh_user` IS THE HEADER KEY THE SSH CLIENT READS - `var user` IS NOT.
#
# MEASURED ON RUN 44611943331 (manjaro), whose failure was NOT a refused port but
#
#	wait for sshd: the port is open but no shell answers: ssh: handshake failed: ssh: unable to
#	authenticate, attempted methods [none password], no supported methods remain
#
# - the daemon reached the guest and offered the WRONG NAME. `require_ssh:` and every `ssh ==`
# step authenticate as `File.SSHUser`, which is parsed from a top-level `ssh_user:` key
# (internal/walk/walk.go) and defaults to `vmuser`. Setting `var user` changes what gets TYPED on
# the console; it does not change who the client logs in as.
user vmuser
var out
  default out/distro.qcow2
  from args.out
password admin1
var user
  default vmuser
  from args.user


# THERE IS NO LOGIN, NO TERMINAL AND NO install HERE, AND THAT IS THE POINT.
#
# This stage used to type its way through a greeter and a dozen commands in a terminal, and
# MEASURED over ten runs of its sibling zorin the virtual keyboard drops and doubles characters
# at line boundaries - one lost `'` leaves bash at a `>` prompt that swallows every later
# command, so `wait for sshd` ran against a machine whose install had never executed.
#
# The disk this leg pulls has had an ssh server put into it BEFORE its first boot, by
# `scripts/seed-ssh.sh` (see the `seed` row in the workflow), together with the offline half of
# vm-configure: hostname, time zone, locale, automatic login and the screen-lock settings.
#
# So the only work left is to boot it and to check that the promise holds: a session, a kernel,
# an account. Not one keystroke.


step "boot the disk"
  boot
    machine "q35,accel=kvm,vmport=off"
    args [["-drive", "if=pflash,format=raw,readonly=on,file=/usr/share/OVMF/OVMF_CODE_4M.fd"], ["-drive", "if=pflash,format=raw,file=OVMF_VARS.fd"], ["-m", "4096"], ["-chardev", "socket,id=qga0,path=qga.sock,server=on,wait=off"], ["-device", "virtio-serial"], ["-device", "virtserialport,chardev=qga0,name=org.qemu.guest_agent.0"], ["-device", "VGA,xres=1920,yres=1080,vgamem_mb=32"], ["-device", "qemu-xhci,id=xhci"], ["-device", "usb-tablet,bus=xhci.0"], ["-device", "usb-kbd,bus=xhci.0"], ["-drive", "file=disk.qcow2,if=none,format=qcow2,discard=unmap,id=target"], ["-device", "virtio-blk-pci,drive=target,bootindex=0"], ["-audiodev", "none,id=snd0"], ["-device", "ich9-intel-hda"], ["-device", "hda-duplex,audiodev=snd0"], ["-netdev", "tap,id=net0,ifname=qemutap0,script=no,downscript=no"], ["-device", "virtio-net-pci,netdev=net0,mac=52:54:00:56:4d:01,romfile=,host_mtu=1450"]]
    timeout 900
# THE GREETER IS ASKED FOR BEFORE ANYTHING IS CLICKED, BECAUSE IT IS NOT THERE YET.
#
# MEASURED ON RUN 44472625613, whose recording is BLACK at 15 seconds and shows the greeter at
# 22: the clicks and the `type:` that followed all landed on nothing, so the password field kept
# its "Password" placeholder and `wait for the desktop` expired after 15 minutes. Every step below
# carries `optional: true`, which is what let the miss through silently - an optional step that
# misses is indistinguishable from one that was not needed.
#
# THE BAND IS THE GREETER'S OWN MIDDLE: the user tile and the password field, x 740..1340 and
# y 470..770. Read back from that recording at scale 2 it yields "Password vmuser"; at scale 1 it
# yields nothing, which is why the scale is 2 and not the default.
# THE GREETER IS RECOGNISED BY THE ONE WORD IT PRINTS LARGE, AND THE GUARDS READ THE SAME BAND.
#
# MEASURED ON RUN 44937306658, whose recording at a third of its length is zorin's own greeter:
# `vmuser` above a focused "Password" box, and the screen BLACK at the end - this guest blanks its
# display exactly as cachyos does.
#
# TWO FAULTS, BOTH ALREADY MEASURED ON ITS SIBLINGS:
#
#   "Password" is a PLACEHOLDER inside a white input field, and the reader does not see it at this
#   size - cachyos's own log shows `see: 4 word(s): hs vmuser ES £3` where the field was plainly on
#   screen. A loop requiring both words could only time out.
#   `esc` IN THE LOOP closes a greeter that is already drawn - cachyos's recording showed the screen
#   returning to the clock after every pass.
#
# And the guards carry the loop's own rectangle: a `when:` without `rect:` reads every pixel, where
# the tile's name is too small - the fault that made cachyos skip its whole login.
# THE GREETER SHOWS THE FULL NAME AND A USER-CHOOSER, NOT A PASSWORD BOX.
#
# MEASURED ON RUN 44948032400's zorin recording, at half its length: GDM draws ONE tile reading
#
#	VM User
#	Not listed?
#
# - the FULL name, not the account - with NO password field until the tile is clicked. So a loop
# waiting for the word `vmuser` can never be satisfied on this screen, and the previous version did
# exactly that for sixty attempts.
#
# THE TILE IS CLICKED FIRST (its box is x 800..1115, y 451..522 on this 1920x1080 frame, centre
# 960,486), and the password box is then waited for by the placeholder the siblings use.


step "wait for sshd"
  repeat
    until machine_ssh
    max 60
    pause 10


step "prove the kernel over ssh"
  ssh "uname -a"
  timeout 120


step "prove the account over ssh"
  ssh "id -un; hostname"
  timeout 120


step "ask the guest to power off"
  ssh "printf '%s\\n' '{{ password }}' | sudo -S -p '' poweroff"
  timeout 300


step "wait for the machine to stop"
  wait_until stopped
  timeout 300


step "publish the disk"
    save "{{ out }}"
